# Build products only.
#
# The release artefact - <id>.owl at the project ROOT, written by
# `make prepare_release` - is deliberately not here. That one is the
# product, and ODK projects commit it so a PURL resolves to something.
#
# Import modules under src/ontology/imports/ are not here either. A
# module is not reproducible output: it is a few dozen axioms this
# project chose to copy from a much larger ontology at a particular
# release. Ignore it and the catalog entry beside it points at a file
# nobody else has.
#
# src/ontology/mirror/ IS ignored, unlike imports/. A mirror is a
# downloaded copy of an upstream ontology - a large one is hundreds of
# megabytes - and it is reproducible from the source each term list
# records. Project > Refresh imports... rebuilds it. The modules under
# imports/ are NOT reproducible that way, which is why those are
# committed and this is not.
src/ontology/mirror/
tmp_*
report.tsv
validate-profile.txt
# robot verify writes one CSV per failing query into src/ontology.
src/ontology/*.csv
*.bak
src/ontology/pizza.owl
